WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.367
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:04.667
Thank you for being here.

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:06.701
Thank you for watching our show.

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:10.100
Let's get to some news.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.801
Well, guys, earlier today
President Biden was in Brussels

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:16.968
to meet with NATO leaders for
an emergency summit on Russia.

00:00:16.968 --> 00:00:19.734
When they voted on a resolution
to condemn Putin,

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:22.968
30 leaders voted "yea," and one
office plant voted "nyet."

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:27.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:29.634
Anyone see that plant walk?
-Yeah.

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:32.100
-Yeah, it was an emergency
summit, but don't worry.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.534
NATO leaders still had time
for a family photo.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:35.901
Here it is.

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:38.100
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.968
Looks like the sales team at
a Honda dealership, doesn't it?

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:42.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:44.801
I'm expecting them to all
say together,

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:46.601
"We're ready to serve you."

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:48.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:50.334
Can we see it again?

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:51.734
Yeah.

00:00:51.734 --> 00:00:53.334
It's a very diverse group.

00:00:53.334 --> 00:00:54.934
There are suits of every color.

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:56.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:58.868
Yeah, that's either a NATO
summit or a conference for

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:00.734
"men who don't know what to do
with their arms" photo.

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:02.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:10.934
Can we see the photo
just one more time?

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:12.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:17.767
♪♪

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:20.000
There we go.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.300
Kind of doing his own thing.
-Yeah.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:25.234
-Well, changing gears,
this morning the "Today" show

00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:27.567
investigated the dangers
of the metaverse.

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:29.534
And they even sent
one of their reporters in

00:01:29.534 --> 00:01:31.467
to see what kind of activity
goes on in there.

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:32.667
Let's see how that went.

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:34.667
-We wanted to see the concerns
for ourselves,

00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:37.601
so I put on a headset and
entered the metaverse.

00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:39.133
That blue robot is me.

00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:41.400
There we entered
a virtual strip club,

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.634
created and uploaded
by another user.

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:46.968
-I am a reporter, yes, trying to
understand the metaverse.

00:01:46.968 --> 00:01:49.400
-[ High-pitched voice ] Oh, you
should not have come in here.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:53.033
-Oh, boy.

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:55.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:57.467
-Amazing!

00:01:57.467 --> 00:02:00.267
Billions spent on technology
so a cartoon weasel

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:01.834
can kick you out of
a fake strip club.

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:03.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:04.868
[ High-pitched voice ] You
should not have come in here.

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:06.334
Oh, no.

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:08.601
Put your hands together
for Cinnamon, everybody.

00:02:09.367 --> 00:02:11.534
[ Normal voice ] Some business
news -- due to a shortage of

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:14.200
ingredients, General Mills
is struggling to supply

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.567
grocery stores with
Totino's Pizza Rolls

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:18.067
and Pillsbury Cookie Dough.

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:19.234
[ Audience ohs ]
-Oh.

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:20.934
-It's serious.
As soon as he heard, Biden

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:22.801
called NATO back for
another emergency summit.

00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:24.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:27.167
Honestly, when I heard there was
a T.P. shortage,

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:28.767
I wasn't thinking
Totino's Pizza.

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:30.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:31.934
Right now General Mills is like,

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:34.267
"Hey, but we still have plenty
of Fiber One bars.

00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:37.567
Hello? Anyone?

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:41.100
Anyone want to gnaw on
a Fiber One bar?"

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:47.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:51.701
One vote said, "Nyet."
One office plant said, "Nyet."

00:02:51.701 --> 00:02:54.234
-It was a spy. It was a Russian
spy, is what you're saying.

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:55.701
-What's that?
-It was a Russian spy

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:57.200
in that plant.
-Oh, is that correct?

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.067
-Yeah, that's what it was.
That's why it said, "Nyet."

00:02:59.067 --> 00:03:01.467
-Oh, so you're saying it's
"30 world leaders said yes."

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:03.300
And then one office plant
said --

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.434
-"Nyet," which is "no"
in Russian.

00:03:05.434 --> 00:03:06.834
-Yeah, and it was --
But a plant --

00:03:06.834 --> 00:03:09.467
-So you're implying that it was
a spy in that plant.

00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:10.634
That's what makes it
so humorous.

00:03:10.634 --> 00:03:11.901
That's what I love about it.

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:16.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:18.267
Topical.

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:20.033
-Yep, it is.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.367
Hey, this is big though, guys.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.934
Yesterday CEOs of every major
U.S. airline called on

00:03:23.934 --> 00:03:26.367
President Biden to drop
the federal mask mandate.

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:28.834
-Ooh.
[ Applause ]

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:31.467
-Each airline actually released
its own statement about it.

00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:33.067
Take a look.
American Airlines said,

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:36.100
"We've complied with the mask
mandate long enough."

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:39.534
United said, "It's time for
a return to normalcy."

00:03:39.534 --> 00:03:42.567
Spirit Airlines said, "Wait,
there was a mask mandate?"

00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:51.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:54.267
And Delta said, "We believe
vaccine numbers are high enough

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:55.701
to drop the mask policy."

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:58.400
Then Spirit said, "Does
duct tape count as a mask?

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.667
'Cause if so, we've been masking
tons of people."

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.367
JetBlue said, "We look forward
to seeing our passengers'

00:04:04.367 --> 00:04:05.901
smiling faces again."

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:08.300
And finally, Spirit said,
"Passengers can smile?

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.534
Oh, now I've heard everything."

00:04:09.534 --> 00:04:10.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:14.601
Pretty out of the loop,
I don't know.

00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:17.200
Hey, get this, I saw that Uber
has reached a deal

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:20.501
to list all New York City taxis
on its app.

00:04:20.501 --> 00:04:22.601
And this makes sense --
they hashed out the deal

00:04:22.601 --> 00:04:24.901
by screaming at each other
through open car windows.

00:04:24.901 --> 00:04:26.901
"You want to sign the deal?
You sign it!"

00:04:26.901 --> 00:04:29.300
You can't park there!
Sign the deal! You" --

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.234 --> 00:04:34.167
Hey, here's some good news.
I read that as kids

00:04:34.167 --> 00:04:37.834
return to the classroom,
their test scores are going up.

00:04:37.834 --> 00:04:41.601
It's a really nice way of saying
we all failed at homeschooling.

00:04:41.601 --> 00:04:43.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.067 --> 00:04:45.067
Yep, first graders are already
coming home like,

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:46.334
[English accent] "Mother,
father, your homeschooling

00:04:46.334 --> 00:04:47.734
efforts were rather deficient."

00:04:47.734 --> 00:04:50.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.067 --> 00:04:52.100
[ Normal voice ]
I heard a new report about

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:54.701
where people like to eat food
in their house.

00:04:54.701 --> 00:04:57.300
And the results might surprise
you. Check it out.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.467
-According to a new survey
in the U.K.,

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:04.067
more than one in five people say
they snack in the bathroom.

00:05:04.067 --> 00:05:07.767
18% confessed they enjoy
their treats on the toilet.

00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:09.567
-No!
-What?!

00:05:09.567 --> 00:05:10.734
-You know what?

00:05:10.734 --> 00:05:12.267
Just take me back
to the metaverse.

00:05:12.267 --> 00:05:13.634
I think I like that.

00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:16.400
[ High-pitched voice ]
"Welcome back, Mr. Fallon.

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:20.033
Here's 70 Jimmy bucks for you
to make it rain."

00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:22.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.267 --> 00:05:24.267
[ Normal voice ] Finally,
researchers say that they're

00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:26.534
getting closer to producing
the first ever

00:05:26.534 --> 00:05:28.968
birth control pill for men.
-Ooh.

00:05:28.968 --> 00:05:33.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:39.901
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:05:39.901 --> 00:05:42.734
-That's better than the original
form of male birth control --

00:05:42.734 --> 00:05:43.968
dress socks with sandals.

